---

<Layout
  title="IELTS and CELPIP Blog | Strategy Guides and Exam Tips"
  description="IELTS and CELPIP strategy guides, exam tips, and practical articles for writing, speaking, reading, and listening improvement."
  type="page"
  keywords={pageKeywords}
  structuredData={pageStructuredData}
>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: var(--s-6);">
    <div class="hero" style={`--hero-bg: url('/heroes/blog.webp');`}>
      <div class="hero-content">
        <h1 class="ic-display">IELTS and CELPIP articles</h1>
        <p>
          Use the blog when you need one strong explanation of one task, one mistake pattern,
          or one study decision. The goal is not to read everything. The goal is to read the
          right page next.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="height: var(--s-6);"></div>

    <div class="grid grid-3 blog-start-grid">
      {startCards.map((card) => (
        <article class="surface blog-start-card">
          <h2 class="ic-display" style="margin-top: 0;">{card.title}</h2>
          <p>{card.text}</p>
          <a href={card.href} class="btn btn-ghost">{card.label}</a>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div style="height: var(--s-6);"></div>

    <div class="surface feature blog-featured">
      <div class="grid grid-2" style="align-items: center; gap: var(--s-4);">
        <div>
          <div class="blog-card-tag ic-eyebrow">Featured</div>
          <h2 class="ic-display" style="margin-top: 0;">{featuredArticle.title}</h2>
          <p style="color: var(--text-muted);">{featuredArticle.description}</p>
          <div class="blog-card-meta">
            <span>{featuredArticle.meta}</span>
          </div>
          <a href={featuredArticle.href} class="btn btn-primary ic-btn">Read article</a>
        </div>

        <div class="blog-featured-note">
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--text-muted);">
            {featuredArticle.note}
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="height: var(--s-6);"></div>

    <div class="surface" style="padding: var(--s-5); margin-bottom: var(--s-6);">
      <h2 class="ic-display" style="margin-top: 0;">How to use this blog well</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-3 blog-start-grid" style="margin-top: var(--s-3);">
        <article class="card">
          <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">1. Pick one score problem</h3>
          <p class="muted">For example: weak introductions, repetitive vocabulary, unfinished speaking answers, or slow reading timing.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">2. Read one article only</h3>
          <p class="muted">If you open too many pages, everything starts to blur. One careful read is stronger than five quick ones.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">3. Return to practice</h3>
          <p class="muted">The blog explains the idea. Your next step should be a lesson, a writing task, or a speaking attempt.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="ic-display">Recent articles</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-3 blog-article-grid" style="gap: var(--s-3); margin-bottom: var(--s-6);">
      {recentArticles.map((article) => (
        <article class="card blog-card">
          <div class="blog-card-tag ic-eyebrow">{article.tag}</div>
          <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">{article.title}</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--text-muted); flex: 1;">{article.description}</p>
          <div class="blog-card-meta">
            <span>{article.date}</span>
            <span>{article.meta}</span>
          </div>
          <a href={article.href} class="btn btn-ghost">Read</a>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-2 blog-task-groups" style="gap: var(--s-4);">
      {taskGroups.map((group) => (
        <section class="surface blog-task-group">
          <h2 class="ic-display" style="margin-top: 0;">{group.title}</h2>
          <div class="stack" style="gap: var(--s-2);">
            {group.links.map((link) => (
              <a href={link.href} class="blog-task-link">{link.label}</a>
            ))}
          </div>
        </section>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div style="height: var(--s-6);"></div>

    <div class="surface blog-cta">
      <h2 class="ic-display" style="margin-top: 0;">Want the new articles without checking the site every day?</h2>
      <p style="max-width: 72ch; margin: 0 auto;">
        The newsletter pulls together the newest lessons, social posts, and study suggestions in one weekly digest.
      </p>
      <div class="cluster" style="justify-content: center; margin-top: var(--s-3);">
        <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Join the newsletter</a>
        <a href="/about" class="btn btn-ghost">About the teacher</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="height: var(--s-6);"></div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .blog-start-grid {
    gap: var(--s-3);
  }

  .blog-start-card,
  .blog-task-group {
    padding: var(--s-4);
    border-radius: 16px;
  }

  .blog-featured {
    padding: var(--s-5);
  }

  .blog-featured-note {
    background: var(--accent-light);
    padding: var(--s-5);
    border-radius: 16px;
  }

  .blog-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .blog-card-tag {
    display: inline-block;
    width: fit-content;
    background: var(--accent-light);
    color: var(--accent);
    padding: var(--s-1) var(--s-2);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    margin-bottom: var(--s-2);
  }

  .blog-card-meta {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--s-2);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--s-2);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .blog-task-link {
    display: block;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface) 82%, white 18%);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .blog-task-link:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .blog-cta {
    padding: var(--s-5);
    text-align: center;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(23, 54, 86, 0.05) 0%, rgba(217, 72, 72, 0.08) 100%);
    border-radius: 18px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .blog-start-grid,
    .blog-article-grid,
    .blog-task-groups {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr !important;
    }
  }
</style>
